  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "The sum of three numbers in an arithmetic progression is $-3$, and their product is $8$. Find the numbers.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p5-q8-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "-4,-1,2",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", or in reverse order.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p5-q8-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Write the terms as ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "a-d,a,a+d",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "; the sum gives ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "a=-1",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and the product gives ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "d^2=9",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let the terms be $a-d,a,a+d$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3a&=-3\\\\a&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nUsing their product,\n$$\\begin{align*}(-1-d)(-1)(-1+d)&=8\\\\-(1-d^2)&=8\\\\d^2-1&=8\\\\d^2&=9\\\\d&=\\pm3\\end{align*}$$\nThe numbers are $-4,-1,2$, or $2,-1,-4$ in reverse order.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
